# Item 2 stage S2 (extract-design plan sections 4, 9 and 10): G1's split world of the KEM-ideal branch equals the correlated family's random game on the compiled root client (prefix, CCA evaluation, native game state and public table internalized; no candidate argument), hence the cached-root game with real Expand; the root client makes at most 1 + qFinish root requests (hidden reads at the Server's resumption and at grouped Beacon finishes, continuation bound inherited along the scan); expanded_uniform_bound gives the uniform-root world at the sum of 1 + qFinish one-query HMAC PRF advantages.

